    "result_text": "I implemented `complete_paragraph` in `app/tgi.py`, but it hasn't been run against a TGI server. The only test just checks that the module imports, and it passes. So the request itself, including the stop behaviour, is unverified.\n\n```python\ndef complete_paragraph(endpoint_url: str, prompt: str) -> str:\n    \"\"\"Continue `prompt` up to the end of the current paragraph (first blank line).\"\"\"\n    client = InferenceClient(model=endpoint_url)\n    generated = client.text_generation(\n        prompt,\n        max_new_tokens=200,\n        stop=[\"\\n\\n\"],\n        return_full_text=False,\n    )\n    return generated.rstrip()\n```\n\n- **Stop sequence:** it uses `stop=[\"\\n\\n\"]`, not `stop_sequences`. The pinned huggingface-hub 2.0.0 no longer accepts `stop_sequences`, and I checked the installed `text_generation` signature to confirm that `stop` is the parameter to use.\n- **Prompt excluded:** `return_full_text=False` is set explicitly so the prompt is never included in what comes back.\n- **Trailing whitespace:** `.rstrip()` removes it. That also covers TGI including the `\"\\n\\n\"` stop sequence at the end of its output.\n- **Style:** the client setup follows the same pattern as `app/titles.py`, and no dependencies were added."
